d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341109" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-340665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-340665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the sine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}-\\frac{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{(s+3\\text{i})-(s-3\\text{i})}{(s-3\\text{i})(s+3\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{6\\text{i}}{{s}^{2}+9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-340665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4575261e49ce28ccfc3540c372e6382d7c68a7f7e64c7164d3b331ee91b19d36"} {"question" "q-340665" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-340665" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}-9}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}"]]