category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the sine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)=\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}-\\frac{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)} & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{(s+12\\text{i})-(s-12\\text{i})}{(s-12\\text{i})(s+12\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{24\\text{i}}{{s}^{2}+144}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4575261e49ce28ccfc3540c372e6382d7c68a7f7e64c7164d3b331ee91b19d36"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{12s}{{s}^{2}+144}"] ["math" "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144}"] ["math" "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}-144}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+144}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-144}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s>-12"] ["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>12"] ["math" "s\\ge -12"] ["math" "s\\ge 0"] ["math" "s\\ge 12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341127" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)=\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-8},\\,s>8 \\\\ L{{e}^{-8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+8},\\,s>-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{s+8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+8)-(s-8)}{(s-8)(s+8)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{16}{{s}^{2}-64}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}-64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (8,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-8,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(8,\\infty )\\cap (-8,\\infty )=(8,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/state.json" "file_sha256" "89f9df8a11d6863461ca705818890b4a7d6909e6d9f6ddc5a4f2bade54fbb890"} {"question" "q-341140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4575261e49ce28ccfc3540c372e6382d7c68a7f7e64c7164d3b331ee91b19d36"} {"question" "q-341140" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category